meta {
  name: Transfer - Repeat
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/{{transferId}}/repeat
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "repeatReason": "Sample clotted"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
}

docs {
  Receiving branch: ask the sender to re-collect (transfer RECEIVED or ACCEPTED -> REPEAT).

  For an INTERNAL transfer the test goes back to the sender in the same transaction:
  - from RECEIVED: the sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT (its
    report never left the sender and stops being hidden);
  - from ACCEPTED: the receiving copy is voided, the report returns to the sender,
    and the original sample goes to REPEAT. Refused (422 SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED) if the
    report has been worked on at the receiving branch.
  The transfer update is conditional on its current status: a concurrent change makes
  this fail with 422 INVALID_TRANSFER_TRANSITION instead of overwriting it.
  The sender's referring panel (B2B) is notified once the change has committed.
  Internal branch transfer rules (manager flow 2026-09-29):
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER's Technician
    worklist hides its report (list, counts, detail, history, every write, the five
    secondary worklists, attachments, inventory usage, analyser results). It behaves
    as "Lab report not found" (404 LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND) for the sender.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.
}
